{"id":"musee-dorsay","name":"Musée d'Orsay","qid":"Q23402","country":"France","locality":"7th arrondissement of Paris","lat":"48.859972","lon":"2.326527","built":"1986","year":1986,"year_text":"1986","century":"20th century","era":"20th century and later","period":"","date_basis":"Wikidata, inception","style":"","heritage":"","type":"art museum; national museum","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Musée_d'Orsay","text":"The Musée d'Orsay (UK: MEW-zay dor-SAY, US: mew-ZAY -⁠, French: [myze dɔʁsɛ]; English: Orsay Museum) is a museum in Paris, France, on the Left Bank of the Seine. One of the largest art museums in Europe, it is housed in the former Gare d'Orsay, a Beaux-Arts railway station built from 1898 to 1900. The museum holds mainly French artworks (including works by France-based foreign artists) dating from 1848 to 1914, including paintings, sculptures, furniture, and photography.","text_source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mus%C3%A9e_d%27Orsay","text_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","real":[{"id":"gh-3301ea025159","w":800,"h":1200,"title":"Musée d'Orsay 12 November 2008.jpg","o":"gh-3301ea025159.jpg","credit":{"text":"Space Julien","license":"CC BY 2.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mus%C3%A9e_d%27Orsay_12_November_2008.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}},{"id":"gh-eabf9fc570bb","w":1200,"h":800,"title":"Gare d'Orsay (49570190081).jpg","o":"gh-eabf9fc570bb.jpg","credit":{"text":"Cheng-en Cheng from Taichung City, Taiwan","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gare_d%27Orsay_%2849570190081%29.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}},{"id":"gh-6f03b4af66a9","w":1200,"h":675,"title":"Paris - Orthophotographie - 2018 - Palais du Louvre 02.jpg","o":"gh-6f03b4af66a9.jpg","credit":{"text":"Institut national de l'information géographique et forestière","license":"Licence Ouverte","license_url":"https:/